-- title:
--   Birkhoff's far-side inequality $v_1+2x_2>0$ along far shooting arcs
-- statement:
--   Fix $0<\mu<1$ and a Jacobi energy $-c$ below the first critical value. Let $\Sigma_{\mu,c}$ be the selected Levi-Civita component and $\varphi$ a continuous flow on it generated by the Hamiltonian vector field of $K_{\mu,c}$. Write $(x_1,x_2)$ for the physical position relative to the primary and $(v_1,v_2)$ for the physical (Jacobi) velocity. Let $F(r)$ be the perpendicular far start at $z=(0,r)$.
--
--   **Birkhoff's far-side inequality.** Let $r>0$, and suppose that $F(r')$ admits a far shooting arc for every $0<r'\le r$. Then along the far shooting arc of $F(r)$, of length $\tau$,
--   $$v_1+2x_2>0\qquad\text{for all } 0<t<\tau.$$
--
--   Along the flow, $\frac{d}{dt}(v_1+2x_2)=\Omega_x$ in physical time, and the quantity starts at $0$ on the far axis. On the far side of the primary $\Omega_x>0$, except in a thin region adjacent to the vertical line $x_1=0$, where $\Omega_x=-\mu(1-r_2^{-3})<0$ off the axis. So the inequality is not a pointwise monotonicity; it expresses that far arcs of the initial family reach that line before losing the margin. Numerically, $v_1+2x_2\ge 2.6\,|x_2|$ along all far arcs of the initial family, for $\mu\in[0.001,0.999]$ and a range of energies.
--
--   The inequality gives $v_1>2|x_2|$ along far arcs. Its limit form excludes both a vanishing horizontal velocity and a vertical tangency at the end of the far family, and it reduces the far compactness lemma `birkhoff_far_arc_limit` to this statement.
-- source:
--   Birkhoff 1915, The restricted problem of three bodies, §§16–18 (Collected Mathematical Papers Vol. 1, pp. 731–741); Liu–Salomão, arXiv 2506.17867v2, §5

import Definitions.Def_BirkhoffShootingArcs

namespace BirkhoffGlobalSection

theorem birkhoff_far_arc_velocity_bound (μ c : ℝ)
    (hμ0 : 0 < μ) (hμ1 : μ < 1)
    (hc : belowFirstCriticalValue μ c)
    (φ : Flow ℝ (LeftEnergyState μ c))
    (hφ : IsLeviCivitaHamiltonianFlow μ c φ)
    (r : ℝ) (hr : 0 < r)
    (hgood : ∀ r' ∈ Set.Ioc 0 r, ∃ x : LeftEnergyState μ c, (x : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c r' ∧ ∃ τ : ℝ, IsFarShootingArc φ x τ)
    (x : LeftEnergyState μ c) (hx : (x : Phase) = farShootingStart μ c r)
    (τ : ℝ) (harc : IsFarShootingArc φ x τ) :
    ∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo 0 τ,
      0 < jacobiVelocity (leviCivitaToJacobi μ ((φ t x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase)) 0 +
        2 * relativePosition μ ((φ t x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 1 := by sorry

end BirkhoffGlobalSection
